formula:
\mathrm{AI}_c = 100 \, \frac{g_{cc}}{\max g_{cc}}
\max g_{cc} = 2s(s-1) + \begin{cases} 0 & m = 0 \\ 2m - 1 & 0 < m \le s \\ 2m - 2 & m > s \end{cases}
\qquad s = \lfloor \sqrt{n_c} \rfloor, \quad m = n_c - s^2

metrics.use:
The differences are per cell: the cell size is not used, so the value depends on the resolution; divide by the cell
size to get a true gradient. geodiv divides by the number of all cells, including those without both neighbours;
Terraflux divides by the number of cells that have them.

The scaling uses the whole raster, so the value of a cell depends on the extent. Positive means convex (the cell is
higher than its neighbours), negative concave. spatialEco divides by 9 and subtracts 1 through operator precedence;
Terraflux corrects that.
